Q: Error 500 when loading database in codeigniter A: <p>Use these settings:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>$db['default']['password'] = '';
$db['default']['dbdriver'] = 'mysqli';
</code></pre>

Q: Cannot use $this-&gt;load property when CodeIgniter controller class name matches method name A: <p>This is a PHP "limitation" - it is a backwards compatibility feature for PHP 4, where you don't have <code>__construct()</code> and a method name matching the class name is executed as a class constructor.</p>

<p>You probably could go around that if you put a PHP5-style constructor to be called instead, just make sure to call the parent one in it:</p>

<pre><code>public function __construct()
{
     parent::__construct();
}
</code></pre>

<p>Also, this wouldn't be the case if you're inside a namespace, but CodeIgniter currently doesn't utilize those for compatibility with older PHP versions.</p>
